/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Torque T is the twisting effort the crankshaft delivers, in N·m.
   - P is brake power in W; T is brake torque in N·m; N is speed in rev/min; 2π ÷ 60 converts rev/min to rad/s.
   - At 3000 rpm and 150 N·m, P = 2π × 3000 × 150 ÷ 60 = 47.1 kW.
   - Brake mean effective pressure (BMEP) lets engines of different sizes be compared.
   - A fuel meter gives the fuel mass flow ṁf, usually in kg/h.
   - BSFC is in g/kWh; ṁf is in kg/h; P is in kW; 1000 converts kg to g.
   - A small BSFC is good.
   - One kWh is 3600 kJ.
   - ηbth is a fraction; BSFC in g/kWh; CV in MJ/kg; 3600 is kJ per kWh.
   - Indicated power is the power the gas delivers to the pistons.
*/
