/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Here λ (the excess-air ratio) = actual air-fuel ratio ÷ stoichiometric air-fuel ratio; λ = 1.05 means 5 percent more air than the fuel needs.
   - Open loop means the ECU computes an output from its stored calibration alone.
   - Closed loop means a sensor measures the result and the ECU corrects the output.
   - The figure is the block diagram of an engine management system.
   - Signal path.
   - The processor runs its program from flash memory and keeps working values in RAM.
   - Calibration grid.
   - y is the value wanted (for example injector open time in ms); x is the measured speed or load; (x₁, y₁) and (x₂, y₂) are the two neighbouring calibrated cells.
   - Between cells, the ECU interpolates linearly along each axis.
   - Air measurement.
*/
