/* book exam traps: Calling a map-based output closed loop. A table lookup is open loop even though it is electronic; the loop closes only when a sensor measures the result. | Interpolating along the wrong axis. Use the two cells that bracket the measured load in the same speed column. | Mixing milliseconds and percent. Pulse width is a time in ms; duty is that time divided by the cycle time, and a four-stroke cycle is two revolutions. | Treating λ = 1 as the target everywhere. Full load runs rich in open loop, and cranking and warm-up ignore the cold λ sensor. | Thinking limp-home is normal running. It replaces a failed sensor with a substitute value and limits the engine; it keeps the car moving, not clean. */
